-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Decision functions answer `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "means" definition, an "if", "unless", "upon"
--                or "where" not met, a period fixed in the text's own words).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer (a scope limit, a lifted bar that grants nothing, a bare "must" not done).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer (the Court may order otherwise in the interests of justice).
-- The Income Tax Act is not among the sources: the facts of that Act are inputs.
-- PERIODS are counted under O 3 r 3 (lines 323 to 329); the last day is the seam input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.

