`o 47 r 1(1) a request is the subject request` MEANS
    IF `the request was made under section 105D(1)` AND `a power under section 65, 65A or 65B was exercised for the request` AND `the exercise of that power is the subject of the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“subject request” ... means the request made under section 105D(1) for which power under section 65, 65A or 65B was exercised, and the exercise of which is the subject of those proceedings"

