    `o 47 r 5(2)(b) the person from whom the Comptroller obtains the information`
    `o 47 r 5(2)(c) the person in relation to whom information is sought`

-- The period: "at least 28 days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application".  Counted under O 3 r 3(4):
-- the period ends immediately before the hearing date.  The last day is the seam input.
-- COVERS O 47 r 5(2)
-- src:6206 | 5. —(1) An application for permission of the Court under this Order must be supported by an affidavit. (2) The application and supporting affidavit must be filed and served on each of the following persons at least 28 days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application, unless that person is the applicant himself or herself: ( a )
-- src:6207 | the Comptroller;
-- src:6208 | ( b )
-- src:6209 | the person from whom the Comptroller obtains the information;
-- src:6210 | ( c )
-- src:6211 | the person in relation to whom information is sought.
@ref O 47 r 5(2) (src:6206-6211)
`o 47 r 5(2) the period before the hearing` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- "unless that person is the applicant himself or herself": the duty to file and serve on that person does not arise.
-- COVERS O 47 r 5(2)
@ref O 47 r 5(2) (src:6206-6211)
GIVEN person IS A `o 47 r 5(2) the person to be served`
      `the person is the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 47 r 5(2) the duty to file and serve the application and affidavit on the person arises` MEANS
    IF `the person is the applicant`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that person is the applicant himself or herself"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

